frame(x = [1, 2, 3]).variance_test(x)
error[Z0401]: `variance_test` compares the groups of `group:`, which is missing
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:22
  |
1 | frame(x = [1, 2, 3]).variance_test(x)
  |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no `group:`
  |
  = help: write `variance_test(var, group: g)`; the variance of one variable is `variance`

frame(x = [1, 2, 3], g = [1, 1, 1]).variance_test(x, group: g)
error[Z0401]: `group:` of `variance_test` has one level, but the test compares two or more
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:61
  |
1 | frame(x = [1, 2, 3], g = [1, 1, 1]).variance_test(x, group: g)
  |                                                             ^ `g`
  |
  = help: the groups are the values of the variable among the rows kept; `where` or `recode` may give more

