frame(s = ["a", "b"], g = [1, 2]).variance_test(s, group: g)
error[Z0401]: `variance_test` compares the spread of numbers, so `s` must be a Bool, Int or Float variable, but it is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:49
  |
1 | frame(s = ["a", "b"], g = [1, 2]).variance_test(s, group: g)
  |                                                 ^ not numbers
  |
  = help: a text or category variable has no variance; its frequencies are compared by `chi2_test`

frame(x = [1, 2, 3], d = [date("2024-01-01"), date("2024-01-02"), date("2024-01-01")]).variance_test(x, group: d)
error[Z0401]: `group:` of `variance_test` must be a Bool, Int, Str or Category variable, but `d` is a Date
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:112
  |
1 | frame(x = [1, 2, 3], d = [date("2024-01-01"), date("2024-01-02"), date("2024-01-01")]).variance_test(x, group: d)
  |                                                                                                                ^ not a grouping variable
  |
  = help: a group is a value shared by its rows; `bin` makes groups from a number, by breaks or by quantiles

frame(x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], g = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3]).variance_test(x, group: g, method: f)
error[Z0401]: `method: f` of `variance_test` is the ratio of two variances, but `g` has 3 groups
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:79
  |
1 | frame(x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], g = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3]).variance_test(x, group: g, method: f)
  |                                                                               ^ more than two groups
  |
  = help: `method: levene`, the default, and `method: bartlett` compare any number of groups

frame(x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], g = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3]).variance_test(x, group: g, method: bartlett)
