frame(x = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 5.0, 2.0, 2.5], g = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3]).variance_test(x, group: g, center: mean)
error[Z0401]: within every group of `g` the values of `x` lie at one distance from the group's mean, so Levene's test has no variation to compare with
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:81
  |
1 | frame(x = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 5.0, 2.0, 2.5], g = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3]).variance_test(x, group: g, center: mean)
  |                                                                                 ^ no variation within the groups
  |
  = help: this happens when every group holds one value repeated, or two distinct values; the test needs groups whose values differ in more than that

