frame(x = [1, 2, 3, 4], g = [1, 1, 2, 2]).variance_test(x, group: g, method: bartlett, center: mean)
error[Z0410]: `center:` of `variance_test` goes with `method: levene`, not with `method: bartlett`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:96
  |
1 | frame(x = [1, 2, 3, 4], g = [1, 1, 2, 2]).variance_test(x, group: g, method: bartlett, center: mean)
  |                                                                                                ^^^^ a centre, which this method does not use
  |
  = help: Levene's test measures each value's distance from the centre of its group; the other two methods compare the variances themselves

